flow "Timeouts and deadline propagation"
summary "Passes an absolute end-to-end deadline down every RPC hop so expired work cancels immediately instead of triggering cascading timeouts."
tags resilience timeouts microservices
level intermediate
source "https://sre.google/sre-book/addressing-cascading-failures/"
related distributed-systems/hedged-requests distributed-systems/circuit-breaker

node client "Client (500ms)" actor
node gw "API Gateway" service tone=primary
node orders "Orders Service" service
node inv "Inventory Service" service
node db "Inventory DB" db
edge client > gw
edge gw > orders
edge orders > inv
edge inv > db
array budget "Remaining deadline" keys=gw,orders,inv = 500ms 450ms 100ms

scenario propagate "Absolute deadline cancels expired work early"
  step gw-call "Client sets an end-to-end 500ms deadline"
    "Instead of each hop inventing its own timeout, the client attaches an **absolute deadline** (`now + 500ms`). Gateway spends 50ms and forwards `450ms left` to Orders."
    send client > gw "GET /order (500ms)"
    state gw active
    send gw > orders "deadline: 450ms"
    state orders active
  step deep-hop "Orders forwards shrinking budget to Inventory"
    "Orders takes 350ms on earlier calls, leaving only `100ms` for Inventory. Propagating the remaining budget tells downstream services how much time actually matters."
    detail "In gRPC, remaining time travels over the wire in the `grpc-timeout` header so machines do not need synchronized clocks. Servers derive downstream contexts from the incoming `ctx` (never `context.Background()`) and check remaining time before each expensive stage."
    send orders > inv "deadline: 100ms"
    send inv > db "query (100ms max)"
    state inv,db pending
  step clean-cancel "Deadline expires: DB query cancels immediately"
    "At 500ms, the deadline hits `0ms`. Inventory immediately aborts the slow DB query and frees its thread — zero wasted work after the client stopped listening."
    label budget#inv "0ms (expired)"
    state inv,db warning
    send inv > db "CANCEL query"
    send gw > client "504 Deadline Exceeded"
    callout db "Cancelled cleanly; resources freed"

scenario cascading-timeout "Independent timeouts cause zombie work and cascade" from=propagate/gw-call
  step local-timeouts "Each hop uses its own hardcoded 5s timeout"
    "Without deadline propagation, Orders and Inventory each allow a 5s local timeout even though the client gives up after 500ms."
    label budget#orders "5000ms (local!)"
    label budget#inv "5000ms (local!)" with
    send orders > inv "timeout: 5s"
    send inv > db "slow query (5s)"
    state db error
  step client-gives-up "Client times out and retries while zombies run"
    "At 500ms, the client times out and retries — while Inventory and DB keep grinding on the abandoned **zombie request** for 4.5 more seconds."
    detail "Google's SRE Book notes that RPCs earn no credit for late replies: zombie work plus retries exhausts thread pools. Under **bimodal latency**, a timeout orders of magnitude above normal latency lets just 5% stalled requests consume every worker thread and push overall error rates past 80%."
    send gw > client "504 at 500ms"
    send client > gw "RETRY #2"
    state orders,inv,db error
    effect db shake
    callout db "Zombie queries pile up -> outage"
